<title>UK: British Gas down on Hoare Govett comment.</title>
<headline>British Gas down on Hoare Govett comment.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Gas Plc dropped on Tuesday as analysts at ABN AMRO Hoare Govett, the company's broker, cut the stock to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy&quot; and lowered their dividend forecasts for next year, market sources said.</p>
<p>The stock was down 7p at 222 by 0843 GMT in hefty volume of 3.6 million shares.  </p>
<p>For 1997 Hoare Govett cut its dividend estimate to 5p per share from 7-1/4p, sources said. Analysts at the brokerage were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
